node_modules
# Keep environment variables out of version control
.env

/generated/prisma

# Product photographs are tracked deliberately.
#
# Every Product.imageUrl points at a file in uploads/, so ignoring it meant a
# fresh clone rendered a catalogue of broken images with no way to recover the
# pairing — which is exactly what happened when the database was rebuilt and the
# only copy of "which photo belongs to which product" was lost. They are shop
# content, not user data, and 35MB is a fair price for a repository that works
# after `git clone`. Move them to object storage if the catalogue grows large.
#
# uploads-originals/ stays ignored: it holds pre-normalisation copies that
# nothing references and that can be regenerated.
uploads-originals/
